extraction_notes: |
  - The related-skill floor is the book''s own and it is a W.P. floor rather than
    a category-of-skills one: printed 172 says select two W.P.s of choice and
    three other skills, which is five picks with a floor of two from Weapon
    Proficiencies rather than five plus two.
  - "Robot Combat Elite: Power Armor of choice or X-10A, X-60 or X-500" is
    stored as a choice over the three machines the book names. The open half -
    power armour of choice - is not enumerable, and a free-text note would grant
    nothing; the book''s full wording is on the choice so a GM can widen it.
    add-ngr-additional-elite-skills.sql creates the X-60 and X-500 rows.
  - Science is printed as None and is therefore absent from occ_related_skills
    rather than listed empty.
  - Three issued items are choices the book does not resolve and are not
    stubbed: an energy rifle of choice, a sidearm of choice and a vibro-blade of
    choice. The four extra energy clips are issued "for each" of the first two,
    so eight are stored. In the body.
  - The T-11 Enhanced body armour issued alongside the T-10 is NOT stored: it is
    a BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3 vessel, as are the T-Series power armour, the
    X-10A Predator, X-60 Flanker, X-500 Forager and EIR-15 gargoyle bot the
    entry offers on assignment. In the body.
  - The 2 plasma grenades (4D6 M.D.) are not stored, for the same reason as on
    the NGR Intelligence Officer: no catalog row exists, and the Power Armor
    Commando''s list prints 5D6 M.D. for the same item.
  - The standard cybernetics - gyro-compass, clock calendar, universal headjack
    and ear with amplified hearing and an oxygen storage tank - are cybernetics
    rather than carried gear. In the body, with the eighth-level additions,
    which continue onto printed 173 and were read to the end there.
  - starting_money is the first-level savings the book prints, 2D4x1000. The
    2200 credit monthly salary and the 4000 to 7500 a month for 8th level and
    higher are pay rather than starting coin and are in the body.
  - Skill bases are catalog base plus the printed bonus, already added.
---

## Lore

A military specialist in espionage, tracking and guerilla warfare, running seek and destroy, fugitive tracking, sabotage, rescue and reconnaissance. An expert in the combat tactics, habits and resources of the enemy, and in many respects a monster hunter and exterminator. The commando''s services are used by both the intelligence division and the civilian law enforcement branch of the military.

Alignment: Any.

## Rank and pay

Standard military rank, starting as a private. Salary is 2200 credits a month, rising to 4000 to 7500 for eighth level and higher. A pair of commandos share a private four bedroom apartment on or near a base, or the character may pay for a private apartment in town near one.

## Cybernetics

A gyro-compass, clock calendar, universal headjack, and ear with amplified hearing and an oxygen storage tank, all standard to start. Commandos of eighth level or higher are likely to add one or two cybernetic eyes, a bionic arm with two to four weapons or features, and one cybernetic weapon or implant of choice. Others may be purchased, awarded for heroism, or provided for a mission.

## GM Notes

Issued alongside the stored equipment, and not given catalog rows: an energy rifle of choice, a sidearm of choice and a vibro-blade of choice, all unresolved choices; two plasma grenades, which the catalog has no row for; and T-11 Enhanced body armour, which is a vessel-shaped stat block this catalog does not hold.

Available on assignment: additional body armour, weapons, equipment, surveillance and recording gear, cameras, computers and sensory equipment, plus access to the T-Series power armour, the X-10A Predator, X-60 Flanker, X-500 Forager, the EIR-15 gargoyle bot and other transport, at high security clearance. The commando always has priority over power armour, body armour, S.C.U.B.A. equipment, heavy weapons, explosives, cybernetic repairs and weapons.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ngr-intelligence-commando');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ngr-intelligence-commando';

